            <componentInstance>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>decorate</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>richTextValue</name>
                    <value>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-family: &amp;quot;Calibri Light&amp;quot;; font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;FAQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;What is CityView?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;CityView is a geographic visual display of data from 3 major sources of data: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;BGIVE for City/State/National Level Work on Initiatives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;BRM for current/former Mayors, Highlights&amp;nbsp;entered by Program Teams, and Associations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The terminal for Cultural Access and Bloomberg Offices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;What is the goal of CityView?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The goal of CityView is to ensure that program teams and management have a shared place to find a quick high-level overview of BP&apos;s investments in Cities we work with, especially useful before business travel to that city.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;What are teams responsible for adding?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Most of the data is auto-displayed in CityView, however Teams are responsible for adding to the Highlights section; the Highlights section provides detail on our philanthropic investments,&amp;nbsp;high-level programmatic activities, and interactions with prominent&amp;nbsp;officials in that city. Highlights can answer the question:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;If you were about&amp;nbsp;to walk into a room with a mayor, what would you want to be aware of?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Can I add highlights directly from CityView?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;No, CityView only displays the data entered in BRM and BGIVE (or though a feed from the terminal). To add your team&apos;s highlights, navigate to BRM and follow the instructions above for adding Highlights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;How long before my&amp;nbsp;Highlights show in BRM?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Highlights you &quot;submit&quot; to BRM go through the approval process and may take up to one week, but often sooner.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;What should I do if my&amp;nbsp;Highlight is timely?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Enter in BRM the day of the announcement/event, and email Liza Rebold on GI to let her know.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Teams are also responsible for updating BRM with interactions with Mayors and other key officials, how do I determine what belongs in CityView and what belongs in BRM?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Think of BRM as:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt; if another Program Lead/manager was meeting with the same person, even a coffee chat interaction can be a helpful lead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Think of CityView as&lt;/u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;: top of the news hour headlines, big announcements, big headlines, big events.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;How do I get BRM access for additional members of my team?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Email&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:brmhelp@bloomberg.org&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(53, 156, 215); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;u&gt;brmhelp@bloomberg.org&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(127, 127, 127); font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;to request access and cc the team manager. Your request will go through the HR approval process; once approved, you&apos;ll be notified and&amp;nbsp;the BRM team will reach out to schedule a&amp;nbsp;one-on-one training.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentName>flexipage:richText</componentName>
                <identifier>flexipage_richText3</identifier>
            </componentInstance>
